title:: BMOptions
summary:: Documentation BEASTmulch - stores some global options for the BEASTmulch library
categories:: Classes

Description::

BMOptions is a utility class which stores some global options and information for the BEASTmulch library.

CLASSMETHODS::

method:: defaultServerOptions
Returns a new instance of link::Classes/ServerOptions:: using the server related class vars detailed below. These are tweaked for use with the library and may form a more practical starting point than the values found in ServerOptions itself.

INSTANCEMETHODS::
	
method:: version
Returns an Array in the form [majorVersion, minorVersion, subVersion]. Thus 1.0.0 is [1, 0, 0].
		
method:: crossfade
Set or get the default crossfade time in seconds used throughout the library, for example whan adding or removing connections in matrix classes. Default value is 0.1.
				
method:: allowMultipleControlMappings
Set or get a link::Classes/Boolean:: indicating whether BMControl instances can be mapped to more than one object at once. Default value is false.
				
				
Section:: Class Variables for *defaultServerOptions

INSTANCEMETHODS::

The following setters and getters determine the values set in strong::*defaultServerOptions::. See link::Classes/ServerOptions:: for details on their meaning.

method:: numInputBusChannels
Default value is 8.
				
method:: numOutputBusChannels
Default value is 8.
				
method:: numWireBufs
Default value is 512.
				
method:: numAudioBusChannels
Default value is 1024.
				
method:: memSize
Default value is 131072.
	
Examples::

code::
// using defaultServerOptions
o = BMOptions.defaultServerOptions;
o.blockSize = 128; // vary one of the options
s.options = o;
s.boot;
::
